// Title: Suspicious Execution of Shutdown
// Sigma ID: 34ebb878-1b15-4895-b352-ca2eeb99b274
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-01-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: impact, T1529
// Description: Use of the commandline to shutdown or reboot windows
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1529/T1529.md
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/shutdown
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_shutdown_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\shutdown.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/r " or ProcessCommandLine contains "/s ")
